1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,150
Last time, the cover's index
started linking to every recipe.

2
00:00:04,286 --> 00:00:08,646
But once you're on a recipe, there's no
way back, and no way to the next one.

3
00:00:08,711 --> 00:00:11,051
Today we add the links you set yourself.

4
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:16,197
On the Recipe template, I'll start a
small navigation bar along the top:

5
00:00:16,197 --> 00:00:18,710
a text box that says All recipes.

6
00:00:18,819 --> 00:00:20,699
Small, and in the same brown.

7
00:00:23,742 --> 00:00:28,192
Links live at the very bottom of
Element Properties, under Interaction.

8
00:00:28,269 --> 00:00:30,612
The On Click menu has eight targets.

9
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,737
This one is Go to Parent Page.

10
00:00:33,732 --> 00:00:36,442
Notice it never asks for a page number.

11
00:00:36,581 --> 00:00:41,698
This template draws all three recipes, so
a page number would be right on one and

12
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:43,401
wrong on the other two.

13
00:00:43,548 --> 00:00:46,560
Instead, a link names a
relationship, my parent,

14
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:50,198
and each page works out where
that is when you export.

15
00:00:50,404 --> 00:00:51,704
Now sideways.

16
00:00:51,756 --> 00:00:55,484
A Next label on the right, and
its target is Go to Sibling,

17
00:00:55,484 --> 00:01:00,536
with an offset of 1: one step forward
among the pages that share its parent.

18
00:01:00,741 --> 00:01:05,471
And Previous on the left: the same
target, with an offset of minus 1.

19
00:01:05,521 --> 00:01:08,408
It takes a minute to set
up, but it happens once,

20
00:01:08,408 --> 00:01:11,781
on the template, and every
recipe gets the whole bar.

21
00:01:11,986 --> 00:01:14,746
One rule is worth knowing
before you export.

22
00:01:14,843 --> 00:01:19,210
Tomato Soup is the first recipe,
so it has no previous page.

23
00:01:19,353 --> 00:01:22,093
A link like that isn't
left pointing at nothing.

24
00:01:22,194 --> 00:01:24,844
The whole element is left off that page.

25
00:01:25,051 --> 00:01:26,721
Let's export and check.

26
00:01:26,815 --> 00:01:30,665
Page one is still the cover, so
I'll scroll on to Tomato Soup.

27
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,110
It has All recipes, and
Next, but no Previous.

28
00:01:34,316 --> 00:01:38,566
Next takes us to Banana Bread, the
middle recipe, which has both.

29
00:01:38,770 --> 00:01:43,940
And All recipes goes back to the cover,
with its index, ready for the next pick.

30
00:01:44,144 --> 00:01:48,014
Next time: layers, stacking, and
the finer points of styling.
